---
import BaseHead from "../components/BaseHead.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from "../consts";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title="About | Shubham" description="About Shubham - Backend Engineer" />
  </head>
  <body class="w-full max-w-screen-md mx-auto my-4 dark:bg-neutral-800 dark:text-neutral-300 transition-colors duration-300">
    <Header />
    <main class="px-4 md:px-0">
      <div class="w-full h-80 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-12 shadow-lg mt-8">
        <img src="/images/about-hero.jpg" alt="Person sitting on rock near sea" class="w-full h-full object-cover">
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-8 text-neutral-900 dark:text-white">Who I Am</h1>
      
      <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none leading-relaxed text-lg text-neutral-700 dark:text-neutral-300">
        <p>
          Hi, I’m <strong>Shubham</strong> 👋.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm a backend and distributed systems engineer with about 4 years of experience building software that (mostly) doesn't crash. I care deeply about reliability, observability, and making complex systems understandable.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-xl">What I Work On</h3>
        <p>
          My work revolves around data-heavy systems and infrastructure. I prefer simple, boring architectures that are easy to debug over clever, complex ones that are "impressive" until they break at 3 AM. I believe developer experience is a feature, not an afterthought.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-xl">How I Think About Software</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Reliability First:</strong> If you can't trust it, it doesn't matter how fast it is.</li>
            <li><strong>Observability:</strong> I want to know why it broke before the users do.</li>
            <li><strong>Simplicity:</strong> Complexity is the enemy of maintenance.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="font-bold mt-8 mb-4 text-xl">Interests</h3>
        <p>
          When I step away from the terminal, you'll likely find me:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>🚴‍♂️ Riding my bike</li>
            <li>🏏 Watching cricket (and yelling at the TV)</li>
            <li>🌌 Reading about space and physics</li>
            <li>🎵 Listening to music</li>
            <li>🥧 Tinkering with Raspberry Pis and home automation</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
